bmB(){return A.a_J(!0,"Games",A.b([A.Fc(new A.aR0(),"https://github.com/adario/rasterizer_flutter/blob/main/flame_rasterizer/example/lib/stories/games/svg_shooter","    A vertical shooter drawn with SVGs. The player's spaceship is an SVG in\n    colour, and the enemies and the missiles are wireframe SVGs.\n    RasterizerSvgComponent draws them with the renderer that the Renderer knob\n    picks; with Flame SVG, flame_svg's SvgComponent does.\n\n    Move the spaceship by dragging anywhere, or with the arrow keys or WASD.\n    Fire while dragging, or while holding the space bar. Once the game is over,\n    tap to start a new one.\n\n    Waves of enemies fall from the top: two kinds of spaceships, rockets and\n    swinging robots, in random colours. Each enemy that hits the spaceship\n    takes some of its health, which comes back after a while without a hit.\n    The game is over when the health runs out.\n\n    Hundreds of SVGs are on screen at once, each with an SvgHitbox in the shape\n    of its paths. The stars are sprites, and the explosions are particles. The\n    other knobs zoom the camera and change the game's speed; with Flame SVG,\n    the cache knobs set flame_svg's cache. The health, the score and the number\n    of components are at the bottom right. The bar under the game shows the\n    renderer, the frame times and the renderer's own numbers.\n\n    Based on Flame's Rogue Shooter example game.\n  ","Svg Shooter"),A.Fc(new A.aR1(),"https://github.com/adario/rasterizer_flutter/blob/main/flame_rasterizer/example/lib/stories/games/tube_shooter","    A tube shooter in vector lines. Everything in the game, text included, is\n    a Flutter Path. RasterizerPathComponent draws them with the renderer that\n    the Renderer knob picks; with Flame SVG, Flame's PathComponent does.\n\n    Move the ship round the rim of the tube with the arrow keys, A and D, or by\n    dragging left and right. Fire down its lane with the space bar, or while\n    dragging. Enter, or a double tap, purges the tube once a round. Tap or\n    press a key to start a round, and to go on after losing a ship.\n\n    Five kinds of enemies climb the tube. Once they're gone, the ship drops\n    down its lane to the next of eight tubes, and any spike left in that lane\n    destroys it. Each round is 5% faster than the last, and a game that starts\n    at a later level goes as fast as if it had started at the first. After\n    Game Over, a new game starts at the round reached, as fast.\n\n    The game makes some paths again every frame, such as the tube's during the\n    zoom. It shares others among many components, such as the enemies'\n    shapes. With the mesh renderer, the Glow knob makes the lines glow. The\n    Level knob shows the round's level, and starts a new game at the level it\n    picks. The other knobs keep the stars drifting, turn the sounds on and\n    off, zoom the camera and change the game's speed. The bar under the game shows the renderer, the frame\n    times, the renderer's own numbers and the paths made each second.\n\n    Inspired by Atari's Tempest (1981).\n  ","Tube Shooter")],t.Jw))},
